### General tips to shrink “normal” code

| Technique | What it removes | Example |
|-----------|-----------------|---------|
| **Functional patterns** (`map`, `filter`, `reduce`) | Explicit loops | `arr.map(f)` instead of `for v in arr { res.push(f(v)); }` |
| **Destructuring** | Re‑assignments | `const {x,y} = obj;` |
| **Default parameter values** | `if (x == null) x = def;` | `function foo(x = default) {}` |
| **Optional chaining** | Nested `&&` or `if` | `obj?.prop?.subprop` |
| **Using built‑in methods** | Custom mini‑loops | `arr.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)` |
| **Template literals** | String concatenation + ` verbind  | ``${first} ${last}`` |
| **Short‑circuit evaluation** | Ternary for simple conditionals | `condition && doSomething();` |
| **Lazily generated data** | Loading entire data set | Generators (`yield` in Python, `function*` in JS) |

> **Remember:** a concise structure is still readable. Prefer readability over a single‑line “no‑boilerplate” style if it hurts comprehension.
